{title: 375 - Work, for the Night Is Coming}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Work for the night is [Ab]com[Eb]ing, Work through the [Cm]morn[Bb]ing [Eb]hours;
[Eb]Work while the dew [Eb7]is[Ab]spark[Eb]ling; Work [Ab]mi[Eb]d sprin[Bb7]g-in[Eb]g flow'rs.
[Bb]Work when the [Fm]day [C7]grows [Fm]bright[Bb]er, [Eb]Work in the [Cm]glow[F7]ing [Bb]sun;
[Eb]Work for the night [Eb7]is[Ab]com[Eb]ing, When [Ab]man's [Eb]work [Bb7]is[Eb]done.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Work [Ab]for [Eb]the [Cm]night [Bb]is [Eb]coming,
[Eb][Eb7]Work [Ab][Eb]thro' [Ab]the [Eb][Bb7]sunny [Eb]noon;
[Bb][Fm]Fill [C7][Fm]brightest [Bb][Eb]hours [Cm][F7]with [Bb]labor,
[Eb][Eb7]Rest [Ab][Eb]comes [Ab]sure [Eb][Bb7]and [Eb]soon.
[Eb][Ab]Give [Eb]every [Cm][Bb]flying [Eb]minute
[Eb][Eb7]Something [Ab][Eb]to [Ab]keep [Eb][Bb7]in [Eb]store;
[Bb][Fm]Work [C7]for [Fm][Bb]the [Eb]night [Cm][F7]is [Bb]coming,
[Eb][Eb7]When [Ab][Eb]man [Ab]works [Eb][Bb7]no [Eb]more.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Work [Ab]for [Eb]the [Cm]night [Bb]is [Eb]coming,
[Eb][Eb7]Under [Ab][Eb]the [Ab][Eb]sunset [Bb7][Eb]skies;
[Bb][Fm]While [C7]their [Fm][Bb]bright [Eb]tints [Cm][F7]are [Bb]glowing,
[Eb][Eb7]Work [Ab][Eb]for [Ab][Eb]daylight [Bb7][Eb]flies.
[Eb]Work [Ab]till [Eb]the [Cm]last [Bb]beam [Eb]fadeth,
[Eb][Eb7]Fadeth [Ab][Eb]to [Ab]shine [Eb][Bb7]no [Eb]more;
[Bb][Fm]Work [C7]while [Fm][Bb]the [Eb]night [Cm][F7]is [Bb]dark'ning,
[Eb][Eb7]When [Ab][Eb]man's [Ab]work [Eb][Bb7]is [Eb]o'er.
